661:      * be canceled and is also stopped when the backend is closed through {@link #dispose()}. For
662:      * each backend, this method must always be called by the same thread.
663:      *
664:      * @param checkpointId The Id of the checkpoint.
665:      * @param timestamp The timestamp of the checkpoint.
666:      * @param streamFactory The factory that we can use for writing our state to streams.
667:      * @param checkpointOptions Options for how to perform this checkpoint.
668:      * @return Future to the state handle of the snapshot data.
669:      * @throws Exception indicating a problem in the synchronous part of the checkpoint.
670:      */
671:     @Nonnull
